---
import Banner from "../Components/Banner.astro"
import Hbox from "../Components/Hbox.astro";
import Panel from "../Components/Panel.astro"
import Footer from "../Components/Footer.astro"
import "../styles.css"
---

<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<meta charset="utf-8" />
		<link rel="icon" href="/favicon.png" />
		<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
		<meta name="generator" content={Astro.generator} />
		<title>Mr-Chen-Rui</title>
	</head>
	<Banner/>
	<body>
		<Hbox>
			<Panel>
				<h3>
					Hello! :3
				</h3>
				<hr>
				I am a coder, swimmer, 3D modeler, and reader who is against the use of generative AI in coding. 

				<h3>
					About
				</h3>
				<hr>

				<h3>
					Tech Stack
				</h3>
				<hr>
				I often use JS, HTML, and CSS, although Astro is my favorite framework. I also use Vite as a bundler for web development.
				<br>
				I can use Godot and Unity, and can code in Java, Python, and C#. Currently, I'm learning C and C++.
			</Panel>
			<Panel>
				hello
			</Panel>
		</Hbox>
		<Footer/>
	</body>
</html>
<!-- Annoying thing is that in css you must explicitly state height of the parent element if you want 100% height -->
<style scoped>
body{  
	min-height: 100%;
	display: grid;
	grid-template-rows: auto 1fr auto;
}
html{
	height:1px
}

</style>